  "about": "Hand-placed walk links (tools/gen_walk_regions.py): where a walk crosses what the terrain grid can't see (bridges, tunnels, lifts: buildings, WMOs, aren't terrain). Ends in tile coordinates (Atlas: col, row on the map) on the terrain you stand on just outside each mouth, each moved to the nearest chunk you can stand on. Found from the WMO placements (obj0 MODF) and their walkable faces, and the bridge doodads' (MDDF M2) collision faces, against the ADT heights: where a raised deck or a sunken tunnel floor steps onto the terrain; lifts from their shaft and the ground at the top and the foot. Optional \"cost\" (chunks walked, at least the straight distance): a long tunnel's real walk or a lift's wait and ride; optional \"oneway\": true (a to b only). Ordered by inst, then north to south. Check them on the demo's pathing debug (Connectors layer).",
